    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d263">

                <pb facs="0902" n="878" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg878"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">C.F.M. Files: Lot
                    M–88: Box 2061: CFM Documents</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Draft Resolution by the French
                            Delegation to the Council of Foreign
                            Ministers</hi><anchor n="9" xml:id="d263-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C.F.M.(46) 216</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-07-10">10 July, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Germany</hi></p>
                <p>A Committee of qualified experts of the four Occupying Powers shall be instructed
                    to report to the Council of Foreign Ministers by 10th August, 1946 at the latest
                    on the following points: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Steps to be taken to increase the German output of coal;</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>General principles which should govern the allocation of the Germany
                            output, due allowance being made for the coal requirements of liberated
                            Europe.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>The Committee’s report should enable the Council of Foreign Ministers to
                    determine the policy and the general directives to be given to the Control
                    Council in Berlin on these points.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d263-f1" n="9" type="source" xml:id="d263-f1-content">
                <p>This paper was circulated to the Council of Foreign Ministers at its 39th
                    Meeting, July 10, 1946. The subject raised in this paper was discussed by the
                    Council at its 40th Meeting, July 11, 1946. For the United States Delegation
                    Records of the meetings under reference, see <ref target="#pg877">pp. 877</ref>
                    and <ref target="#pg880">880</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
